WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.716
Thumbelina felt like crying.

2
00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:21.943
She was scared, hungry, and lonely.

3
00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:26.150
"I will not cry," she said aloud.

4
00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:28.789
"At least I am free.

5
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.382
No one is trying to catch me."

6
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:33.412
She felt better.

7
00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:37.552
Thumbelina wandered for many days.

8
00:00:37.553 --> 00:00:42.115
It was not easy to survive in the forest.

9
00:00:42.116 --> 00:00:47.497
Thumbelina used a leaf as an umbrella when it rained.

10
00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:53.766
At night she slept on soft moss in a tree root.

11
00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:59.614
Every morning, Thumbelina washed her face with dew from the grass.

12
00:00:59.615 --> 00:01:05.551
Then she'd climb a flower and eat a petal or two.

13
00:01:05.552 --> 00:01:11.314
"I'm tired of eating flowers every day," she said.

14
00:01:11.315 --> 00:01:14.390
She was nibbling on a lily.

15
00:01:14.391 --> 00:01:20.232
"Tired of flowers?" said a red bug with black dots.

16
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:24.085
"Oh, I'm sorry," said Thumbelina.

17
00:01:24.086 --> 00:01:25.846
"I didn't see you.

18
00:01:25.847 --> 00:01:28.312
I'll go to another flower."

19
00:01:28.313 --> 00:01:34.078
"I'm a ladybug. I don't eat flowers," said the bug.

20
00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:37.594
"I eat tiny insects."

21
00:01:37.595 --> 00:01:39.140
"Don't eat me!

22
00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:42.592
I'm not an insect. I'm Thumbelina."

23
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:48.787
"And my name is Ladybird," laughed the ladybug.

24
00:01:48.788 --> 00:01:51.294
"Would you like these insects?

25
00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:53.218
They're very good."

26
00:01:53.219 --> 00:01:57.184
"No, thank you," Thumbelina said quickly.

27
00:01:57.185 --> 00:02:02.154
"How about some blueberries?" said Ladybird, smiling.

28
00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:06.819
"I can show you where they grow. Follow me."

29
00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.034
Thumbelina clapped her hands and said,

30
00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:14.209
"That sounds wonderful. Thank you!"

31
00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:18.742
Suddenly the ladybug opened her wings to fly.

32
00:02:18.743 --> 00:02:22.596
The lily started to move back and forth.

33
00:02:22.597 --> 00:02:27.734
Thumbelina lost her balance and fell off the flower.

34
00:02:27.735 --> 00:02:37.062
"Hey!" She landed on a sand hill and slid down a dark tunnel.

35
00:02:37.063 --> 00:02:40.815
"Enemy alert!" someone shouted.

36
00:02:40.816 --> 00:02:46.113
Thumbelina was inside an anthill.

37
00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:50.400
Many ants were lined up like soldiers.

38
00:02:50.401 --> 00:02:53.314
A big ant pointed at her.

39
00:02:53.315 --> 00:02:56.098
"Get out, stranger!"

40
00:02:56.099 --> 00:03:01.457
"I . . . what happened was …," Thumbelina stammered.

41
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:04.136
"We must protect our queen.

42
00:03:04.137 --> 00:03:08.767
Forward march!" the ant shouted.

43
00:03:08.768 --> 00:03:11.230
"Please, it's all a mistake.

44
00:03:11.231 --> 00:03:14.599
I'll get out," Thumbelina cried.

45
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.609
She tried to climb back up the tunnel.

46
00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:24.519
"This sand is so slippery!" she said, frustrated.

47
00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:29.740
"Capture the enemy!" shouted the ants.

48
00:03:29.741 --> 00:03:35.157
Finally Thumbelina climbed up and out.

49
00:03:35.158 --> 00:03:37.713
She glanced behind her.

50
00:03:37.714 --> 00:03:42.989
It looked like a black wave was coming toward her.

51
00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.276
"What am I going to do?" she cried.

52
00:03:47.277 --> 00:03:52.678
"Keep marching!" shouted the big ant to the others.

53
00:03:52.679 --> 00:03:57.587
Thumbelina turned and ran as fast as she could.

54
00:03:57.588 --> 00:04:00.041
"There are so many of them!"

55
00:04:00.042 --> 00:04:05.364
she screamed, afraid to look behind her again.

56
00:04:05.365 --> 00:04:12.455
Just then Thumbelina saw a small hole in a tree.

57
00:04:12.456 --> 00:04:17.688
She ran inside and hid herself with a fallen leaf.

58
00:04:17.689 --> 00:04:21.781
"Maybe they won't find me here," she gasped.

59
00:04:21.782 --> 00:04:26.386
The ants ran around the tree and kept going.

60
00:04:26.387 --> 00:04:34.458
Their voices faded.

61
00:04:34.459 --> 00:04:39.773
At last Thumbelina could not hear them anymore.

62
00:04:39.774 --> 00:04:47.732
Thumbelina was safe for now.
